        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/iran-closes-strait-of-hormuz-despite-ceasefire-after-continued-israeli-strikes-in-lebanon",
        "orario": "16:26",
        "timestamp": 1781965601,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Iran closes Strait of Hormuz despite ceasefire after continued Israeli strikes in Lebanon Middle East Issued on: 20/06/2026 - 16:26 Modified: 20/06/2026 - 16:31 Iran has closed the strait of Hormuz – citing alleged ⁠violations of a ceasefire agreement ​by the US ‌and Israel. Tehran said the closure was the \"first step\" in response ​to what it described ​as breaches ​of commitments regarding the continuing clashes in Lebanon - and warned ​that further measures would be taken if \"aggression\" continued. Details and analysis by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor Kethevane Gorjestani, and FRANCE 24 correspondent in Tehran, Reza Sayah. Israel strikes Lebanon despite ceasefire, at least 16 killed 20/06/2026 Middle East NGOs in Lebanon denounce Israeli attacks on medics amid ceasefire 20/06/2026 Middle East Could Israel lose Donald Trump’s support by continuing to drop bombs in Lebanon? 20/06/2026 Middle East Hezbollah-Israel flare-up in Lebanon despite ceasefire announced by the USA 20/06/2026 Middle East US-Iran ceasefire negociations underway in Switzerland 20/06/2026 Middle East Residents flee as Israeli strikes target southern Lebanon 20/06/2026 Middle East Israel and Hezbollah say they agree to truce despite renewed attacks 19/06/2026 Middle East Uncertainty remains amid postponed US-Iran talks and continued fighting in Lebanon 19/06/2026 Middle East Israeli military strikes southern Lebanon as US-Iran talks are postponed 19/06/2026 Middle East"
